WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.949
Imagine opening a bank account with a video selfie.

2
00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:08.169
An AI gatekeeper checks: real person, or deepfake?

3
00:00:08.169 --> 00:00:09.900
But does it judge everyone fairly?

4
00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:14.077
A deepfake is an AI-made or altered video.

5
00:00:14.077 --> 00:00:16.302
Detection can fail in two ways:

6
00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:19.592
suspecting a real person, or letting a fake one through.

7
00:00:20.361 --> 00:00:23.436
False alarms could lock legitimate people out.

8
00:00:23.436 --> 00:00:25.961
Missed fakes could help fraudsters slip in.

9
00:00:25.961 --> 00:00:30.580
This paper asks whether those risks are shared equally across demographic groups.

10
00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:35.719
The researchers built FairFaceBench, covering nine world regions,

11
00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:39.694
two gender categories, and seven ways to create fake videos,

12
00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:41.987
from face swaps to talking avatars.

13
00:00:42.711 --> 00:00:46.636
They tested four detectors and compared demographic groups.

14
00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:51.661
Instead of trusting one average score, they checked which groups faced more suspicion,

15
00:00:51.661 --> 00:00:53.574
and where fakes were hardest to spot.

16
00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:57.894
First, new technology exposed blind spots.

17
00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:02.594
Before extra training, all four tested systems struggled with commercial talking

18
00:01:02.594 --> 00:01:06.224
avatars from Veo three point one and Sora two.

19
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:10.394
Second, performance differed across demographic groups.

20
00:01:10.394 --> 00:01:13.119
Some real faces drew more suspicion.

21
00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:17.169
Some generated faces were harder to distinguish from real ones.

22
00:01:17.169 --> 00:01:19.041
Averages can hide these gaps.

23
00:01:19.756 --> 00:01:24.606
Extra training on this diverse benchmark improved all four detectors.

24
00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:27.731
Their weakest demographic groups improved too.

25
00:01:27.731 --> 00:01:31.831
The study measured better separation between real and fake faces,

26
00:01:31.831 --> 00:01:33.240
not perfect detection.

27
00:01:33.894 --> 00:01:36.894
But performance dropped on an older benchmark.

28
00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:39.819
And these were tests on individual video frames,

29
00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:43.780
not a guarantee that an entire identity-checking service is fair.

30
00:01:44.502 --> 00:01:48.952
Trustworthy deepfake detection needs both security and fairness.

31
00:01:48.952 --> 00:01:52.247
Look beyond averages, include diverse people,

32
00:01:52.247 --> 00:01:54.947
and keep testing as deepfakes evolve.

33
00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.142
Better protection should work for everyone.
